# SOFTWARE REQUIREMENT SPECIFICATION (SRS)

## 1. Introduction

### 1.1 Purpose

This Software Requirement Specification (SRS) document describes the functional and non-functional requirements of the Secure Approval-Centric System. The purpose of this document is to clearly define system behavior and constraints before development.

### 1.2 Scope

The system is a web-based application that allows users to submit requests and authorized users to approve or reject them. The system ensures secure authentication, structured workflow management, and status tracking.

### 1.3 Definitions

* Requester: User who submits approval requests.
* Approver: Authorized user who approves or rejects requests.
* JWT: JSON Web Token used for secure authentication.
* COCOMO: Constructive Cost Model used for effort estimation.

---

## 2. Overall Description

### 2.1 Product Perspective

The system is a standalone web application developed using React (frontend), Node.js with Express (backend), and MongoDB (database).

### 2.2 Product Functions

The main functions of the system include:

* User registration and login
* Role-based access control
* Request submission
* Approval/rejection workflow
* Request status viewing
* Logout functionality

### 2.3 User Characteristics

* Users must have basic knowledge of web applications.
* Approvers will have administrative privileges.
* All users must authenticate before accessing system features.

### 2.4 Constraints

* Development must follow Agile methodology.
* Effort estimation must use the COCOMO model.
* Version control must use GitHub.
* Project tracking must use Jira.

---

## 3. Functional Requirements

FR-1: The system shall allow users to register and login using secure authentication.

FR-2: The system shall implement role-based access control (Requester and Approver).

FR-3: The system shall allow requesters to submit requests through a structured form.

FR-4: The system shall allow approvers to approve or reject requests.

FR-5: The system shall display request status to the requester.

FR-6: The system shall record basic activity logs.

FR-7: The system shall allow users to logout securely.

---

## 4. Non-Functional Requirements

### 4.1 Security

* The system must use JWT authentication.
* Passwords must be encrypted.
* Only authorized users can access approval functions.

### 4.2 Performance

* The system should respond within 2 seconds under normal load.
* Database queries must be optimized.

### 4.3 Reliability

* The system should maintain data consistency.
* The system must handle invalid inputs gracefully.

### 4.4 Usability

* The interface must be simple and user-friendly.
* Error messages must be clear and understandable.

---

## 5. Assumptions and Dependencies

* The system will run on a modern web browser.
* Internet connection is required.
* MongoDB server must be operational.

---

## 6. Future Enhancements

* Multi-level approval workflow.
* Email notifications.
* Analytics dashboard.
* Cloud deployment.

---



